-- A tuple whose components are a constructor test of a draw-bound ADT and the
-- ADT itself answers 1.0 at every point, e.g. (True, Face True False), where
-- the value is P(x0 = True) * P(x1 = False) = 0.7 * 0.8 = 0.56: the second
-- component is not constrained at all, as if it were ANY. The
-- same tuple off a neural read of Face answers 0.56 correctly, and so does
-- (True, heard). Found while writing corpus cases for task
-- draw-product-read-enumerated-jointly; docs task
-- tuple-ctor-test-of-shared-draw-wrong-result.
data Face = Face x0::Bool, x1::Bool
main =
  draw heard = Face (Uniform < 0.7) (Uniform < 0.2) in
  (isFace heard, heard)
